        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we recall the following formula:\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}-2at+{a}^{2}=(t-a{)}^{2}\n$$\n\nNotice that we have a perfect square in the parentheses that we can factor as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}-22t+121 & = \\\\ {t}^{2}-22t+{11}^{2} & = \\\\ {t}^{2}-2\\cdot 11t+{11}^{2} & = \\\\ (t-11{)}^{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}-22t+121)-1 & = \\\\ (t-11{)}^{2}-1 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
